Styling the host:


- 🔥A special CSS selector exists to style only the host element. It is called :host, and it comes from
    the Web Component specification:

        :host {
            display: block;
        }

    🔥It will be kept as is for the ShadowDom strategy and rewritten into [_nghost-xxx] if you use
    Emulated.


- To conclude, you don’t have to do much to have perfectly encapsulated styles, because the Emulated
    strategy takes care of this business for us. You can switch the strategy to use the ShadowDom one
    if you target only specific browsers, or None if you don’t want to encapsulate styles. This
    strategy can be tweaked per component, or globally for your whole app in the root module.